  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Hygiene and Sanitation in the Catholic Diocese of Yei, South Sudan.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an 8 months project and was designed based on the information collected during previous project monitoring visits conducted by CAFOD, Caritas Australia and the implementing partner. Additional information was also collected during an assessment conducted in November 2011 by Caritas Yei with support from CAFOD, county authorities and the Relief and Rehabilitation Commission after Caritas Yei requested for support to undertake priority needs assessments to inform the direction of relief and development initiatives in the Diocese.
The project seeks to support an Improved household sanitation and hygiene levels that will lead to reduction in disease outbreaks. The project will contribute towards enabling the communities in the targeted areas of Yei Diocese to live together in a safe and clean environment with dignity.  This will be achieved through the promotion and support of good hygiene and sanitation practices in the communities. This initiative will go a long way reducing water borne diseases as well as increasing the time families, particularly women; have to engage in productive activities thus improving their economic status.</narrative>
  </description>
